namespace Linx {

/**

\addtogroup glossary

@concept LegacyArray
@brief An object with a monadic integral subscript operator and a size.
@see `std::vector`, `Kokkos::Array`, `Sequence`...

@concept Mapping
@brief A function object which takes N integers as arguments.
@see `Image`, `Patch`, `GaussianRng`...

@concept Array
@brief A `Mapping` which manages its memory.
@see `Sequence` (1D), `Image` (ND), `Map` (sparse ND).

@concept Proxy
@brief A `Mapping` which does not manage its memory.

It relies on a parent ND array instead, while altering some of its behaviors; e.g. `Shift`

@concept Reducer
@brief An associative and commutative diadic function which has an identity element.
@see `Min`, `Add`, `Multiply`...

@concept Region
@brief A finite collection of positions, which can be iterated with `for_each()`.
@see `Box`, `Line`, `Path`...

@concept Restriction
@brief A `Proxy` whose domain is a subdomain of its parent's domain.
@see `Patch`, `Selection`.

@concept SizedData
@brief A contiguous data container defined by its size and a pointer to its first element.
@see `Sequence`, `Raster`...

@concept Slicing
@brief An operation consisting in shallow coping a rectangular subregion of an array, returning a new array.

@concept Strided
@brief A `Mapping` whose neighboring elements along each axis have a constant distance in memory.
@see `Sequence`, `Image`, `Shift`...

@concept Window
@brief A `Region` which can be shifted with `operator-` and `operator+`.

*/

}
